# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing derived from the ROM is committed.
#
# The cartridge is copyrighted Sunsoft material. This repository holds only our
# own code: the JavaScript port, the extraction tools, the docs and the tests.
# Everything below is REGENERATED from a ROM you legally own -- see README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The ROM itself, in any of the usual forms. Phase 2 is Gradius on the NES, so
# the iNES/UNIF forms are here too -- a cartridge image never enters this repo
# whatever console it came off.
*.gb
*.gbc
*.nes
*.unf
*.unif
*.sav
*.sym
Vimm's Lair.txt

# Extracted ROM data: level maps, tile graphics, metasprites, song streams
assets/

# Disassembly listings
disasm/
disasm2/

# Ripped graphics, rendered frames, oracle traces (all scratch, all derived)
rip/

# Golden frames are rendered game imagery; hashes and PNGs alike are
# regenerated with `node tools/golden.mjs --update`
#
# NOT anchored. A pattern containing a slash is matched from the REPOSITORY
# ROOT, so plain `tests/visual/golden/` stopped covering the tree the moment
# tests/ moved under games/<id>/ -- and ten golden PNGs would have become
# committable with nothing in the diff or in CI to say so. `assets/` and `rip/`
# above have no slash and were already unanchored, which is why they still
# match at the new depth.
**/tests/visual/golden/
**/tests/visual/diff/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Deployable bundle -- contains ROM-derived assets, regenerate with tools/build-dist.mjs
dist/

# Wrangler's local deploy cache
.wrangler/
